 "label": "Marquetry",
 "category": "Stylize",
 "tags": ["look"],
 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "Cuts the picture from wood veneers and lays it as marquetry: every tone becomes a different species, from dark wenge and walnut through cherry and oak to pale holly, and each piece is cut with its own grain direction so the figure of the wood changes from piece to piece. The lighter pieces are sand shaded, scorched darker along their edges in hot sand the way a marquetarian gives them depth, every joint shows a fine knife line, and the lacquer gives the grain a soft shimmer that changes with the light.",
